## Summary

This makes the Blender to game-engine asset handoff a first-party typed Semwright capability and removes ambient Blender executable discovery from the deep driver.

### Typed GLB handoff

Adds blender.export.glb / driver.blender.export.glb.

The operation:
- exports one exact named collection;
- emits a self-contained GLB 2.0 artifact;
- accepts only meshes, armatures and empties;
- requires parents and armature dependencies to remain inside the collection;
- preserves Blender selection and active-object state;
- uses a private temporary file plus no-clobber publication;
- refuses overwrite, path escape and symbolic output targets;
- validates the GLB header and a bounded artifact size;
- returns relative path, SHA-256, bytes and exported object count;
- is tagged artifact-out:model/3d;
- does not expose generic bpy.ops, Python eval/exec or arbitrary operator invocation.

### Owner-pinned Blender runtime

The deep driver no longer searches /usr/bin, /usr/local/bin or ambient PATH.

It now requires:
- read-only blender-runtime mount containing Blender 4.5.14 LTS resources/libraries;
- blender-executable tool authority for the exact Blender ELF, pinned by SHA-256 and materialized by Driver Host as /plugin/tools/blender.

Startup verifies the portable runtime layout and requires exactly Blender 4.5.14 LTS.

### CI / integration coverage added

The Blender native-integration job is updated to exercise:
- official Blender 4.5.14 archive verification;
- real typed GLB adapter contract;
- portable runtime plus /plugin/tools/blender Bubblewrap preflight;
- Landlock startup with only explicit runtime/tool roots;
- real DriverProvider GLB export, SHA verification and no-overwrite;
- broker/CLI GLB export;
- existing render/save and interactive add-on coverage.

## Local work performed

Per project strategy, no heavy Rust compilation/tests were run locally. Only cheap source sanity checks were run:
- cargo fmt --all -- --check
- generated contract sync check
- JSON validation
- Bash syntax
- Python AST parsing
- git diff --check

Heavy verification is intentionally delegated to GitHub Actions.
